      "message": "I would prefer for Skia not to have any mutable globals at all (and if it does need \"globals\" for them to go on a \"library\" object which stores all the library state and the user sets up and passes back in, like `FT_Library` or something like that (though even this is to be avoided if possible).\n\nMutable globals on a library make it very difficult to use properly, for case studies see `strtok` vs `strtok_r`, using any call in the C standard library that uses the current locale, etc. It\u0027s fine for an application to have these, but a Skia shouldn\u0027t have them.",
